      "explanation": "\\(f(-x)=x^2-x\\), which equals neither \\(f(x)\\) nor \\(-f(x)\\).",
      "id": "m1",
      "sourceRef": "cn-math/cnm_h036_q4#m1",
      "title": "Compare the parity identities"
    },
    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_h035",
        "cnm_071"
      ],
      "explanation": "An even function must satisfy \\(f(-x)=f(x)\\) for every real \\(x\\), while an odd function must satisfy \\(f(-x)=-f(x)\\). A single failed pair can rule out both: \\(f(1)=2\\) and \\(f(-1)=0\\). Since \\(0\\ne2\\) and \\(0\\ne-2\\), the function is neither odd nor even, choice A.",
      "id": "m2",
